    "Name": "Executioner-B",
    "Details": "The progenitor of the Executioner (Gladiator) first seen on the Rasalhague front of the clan invasion, the Executioner-B is slower and more heavily equipped.   When introduced late in the golden century, the Executioner-B looked amazing when viewed from design documents.  However, when on the field, the fixed jump jets, high heat load, and the lack of speed meant the mech was not usable in most situations that an assault mech was called for.  The Prime configuration is equiuped with two Large Pulse Lasers and Ultra AC/2s for range, with an ER PPC backing them up. At point blank the Executioner-B can call upon a mammoth Ultra AC/20.",
